---
# Invite someone — superadmins only.
#
# A page of our own, like Bulk manage beside it: Decap has no way to add one.
# The server decides who may invite (netlify/functions/invite.mjs); this page
# only asks it, and shows the form to a superadmin.
permalink: /admin/invite/index.html
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow, noarchive, noimageindex" />
    <title>Invite someone - Federation Content Manager</title>
    <style>
{{ cmsConfig.inviteStyles | safe }}
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
{% if cmsConfig.proxyUrl != "/api/cms" %}
    <p class="cms-local-banner">
      Local development only — there are no accounts here, so inviting works on
      the live site only.
    </p>
{% endif %}
    <header class="invite-header">
      <a class="invite-back" href="/admin/">&larr; Content manager</a>
      <h1>Invite someone</h1>
    </header>

    <main class="invite" id="invite-app">
      <p class="invite-status" id="invite-status" role="status">Checking your access…</p>

      <form class="invite-card" id="invite-form" novalidate hidden>
        <p class="invite-intro">
          They get an e-mail from Netlify with a link to choose their password.
          Their address is filled in for them. <strong>Netlify's e-mail is titled
          as a password reset</strong> tell them to expect it, and to check spam.
        </p>

        <div class="invite-field">
          <label for="invite-email">E-mail address</label>
          <input type="email" id="invite-email" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="none"
                 spellcheck="false" required aria-describedby="invite-email-error" />
          <p class="invite-error" id="invite-email-error" hidden>Enter an e-mail address, like name@example.com.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="invite-field">
          <label for="invite-name">Name <span class="invite-optional">(optional)</span></label>
          <input type="text" id="invite-name" autocomplete="off" maxlength="100" />
        </div>

        <p class="invite-access">
          They become an <strong>administrator</strong> straight away — they can
          edit, delete and change site settings as soon as they have chosen a
          password.
        </p>

        <button type="submit" class="invite-button" id="invite-submit">Send invitation</button>
      </form>

      <div class="invite-result" id="invite-result" role="alert" hidden></div>
    </main>

    <script>
      window.FED_INVITE_ENDPOINT = "/api/invite";
{{ cmsConfig.inviteScript | safe }}
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
